WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:11.200
Chimpanzees can identify each other by looking
at photographs of their bottoms.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.480
Vultures can turn a dead body into a skeleton
in under five hours.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.109
The Northern Hemisphere is 1.5oC hotter than
the Southern Hemisphere.

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:24.539
A lobster's brain is in its throat.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:31.460
In 1883, a man named Jack Ferry crossed the
English Channel on a floating tricycle.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:37.370
During its restoration in 1982, the Statue
of Liberty's head was accidentally installed

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:39.300
two feet off-centre.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:46.559
Wherever a leaf is in the world, its internal
temperature is always 21 degrees C.

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:52.590
In 1990, there were no roundabouts in the
US; today there are more than 3,000.

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:59.469
There is a 12% chance that a game of Monopoly
will go on indefinitely.

00:00:59.469 --> 00:01:04.910
The crunch of a crisp or an apple in your
mouth is a mini sonic boom.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:10.720
The 'Masters in Lunacy' were Victorian officials
who investigated whether people claiming to

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.240
be insane were faking it.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:19.320
'The Just Missed It Club' was for people who
almost sailed on the Titanic.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:26.460
Two weeks after it sank, it had 118,337 members.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:31.950
At any one time there are 100,000 ships at
sea.

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:39.340
The first telegram—sent on May 24th, 1884
by Samuel B. Morse—read “What hath god

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.340
wrought!”

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:46.549
Blind people are twice as likely to smell
things in their dreams as sighted people.

00:01:46.549 --> 00:02:02.270
There are 60 people in Venezuela whose first
name is Hitler.

